1.4  Additional definitions used in this License:

     "Model" means any trained machine-learning model, including its
     weights, parameters, configuration, and tokenizer or processor
     files, that is distributed by the Licensor as part of the Work.

     "Model Derivative" means any model that is trained, fine-tuned,
     distilled, pruned, quantized, merged, converted, or otherwise
     derived from the Model or from another Model Derivative. For the
     purposes of this License, a Model Derivative is a Derivative Work.

     "Outputs" means the results that the Work or a Model Derivative
     produces when run. Outputs are not restricted by this License, but
     Sections 2.1 and 2.2 continue to govern how You present them to
     End Users.

     "End User" means a natural person who uses the Work, a Derivative
     Work, or a Covered Product through an Interface.

     "Interface" means any screen, web page, command line, voice or
     other means through which an End User interacts with the Work, a
     Derivative Work, or a Covered Product.

     "Interface Provider" means the person or entity that presents an
     Interface to End Users, whether or not it is the same person or
     entity that distributes the Work.

     "Hosted Service" means any offering of the Work, a Derivative Work,
     or a Covered Product to others over a network or as a service,
     without distributing copies of it.

     "Covered Product" means any application, website, or service, taken
     as a whole, that includes, runs, or is built upon the Work or a
     Derivative Work, including as a Hosted Service. A separate product
     that does not include or run the Work or a Derivative Work, and only
     sends or receives data through a public interface, is not a Covered
     Product by that fact alone.

     "Advertisement" means any content presented to End Users in return
     for payment or other consideration from a third party, or to promote
     the products, services, or interests of a third party, in any form
     (display, video, audio, in-stream, sponsored or promoted content,
     affiliate or referral links, or "rewarded" advertising).

     "Essential Functionality" means the features of the Work or Covered
     Product that analyze, correct, or search recitation, at the same
     Model quality offered to paying users. Reasonable fair-use limits
     (such as rate limits, queue priority, absence of service-level
     guarantees or support, and daily or monthly usage caps) are
     permitted, provided they leave the free path usable for regular
     personal study.

