SECTION 2 - ADDITIONAL CONDITIONS

The Licensor, as copyright holder, grants the rights in this License
subject to the Additional Conditions below, imposed pursuant to Section 4
of the Base License. They apply to every use, reproduction, modification,
distribution, and making available (including offering the Work or any
Derivative Work as a Hosted Service) of the Work and of Derivative Works,
by You and by anyone who receives the Work or a Derivative Work from You.

2.1  AI ADVISORY NOTICE

     (a) Duty. You must ensure that every End User of every Covered
         Product is shown the notice in paragraph (b), clearly and
         conspicuously:

           (i)  before first use; and
          (ii)  at all times afterwards, reachable from the main menu or
                an About or Help screen.

     (b) Text and languages. The notice must be shown in each language
         in which the Interface is offered, and always also in Arabic.
         It must be substantially equivalent to the text below and must
         keep all four of its elements: (1) it is an AI model that may
         make mistakes; (2) it is for assistance only and must not be
         relied upon; (3) it is not a replacement for a proficient,
         authorized teacher; and (4) the Quran is received only through
         oral transmission (mushafahah). If versions differ, the Arabic
         text controls. Where the product is not a teacher (for example,
         a search-only tool), "This tool" may replace "This Quranic
         Teacher". Using the official translations that the Licensor
         publishes in the project repository, word for word, satisfies
         the language requirement for those languages.

       EN: "This Quranic Teacher is an artificial-intelligence model that
            may make mistakes. It is intended for assistance only and must
            not be relied upon. It is not a replacement for a proficient,
            authorized teacher, because the Quran is only received
            through oral transmission (mushafahah)."

       AR: "هذا المعلّم القرآني نموذج ذكاء اصطناعي قد يخطئ؛ فهو للإعانة
            فقط ولا يُعتمد عليه، وليس بديلاً عن معلّمٍ مُتقِنٍ مُجاز؛ لأنّ
            القرآن لا يُؤخذ إلا بالمشافهة."

     (c) Who must comply. The duty in paragraph (a) falls on the
         Interface Provider. If You distribute the Work or a Derivative
         Work as a library, API, or other component without presenting
         an Interface to End Users, You must include this requirement
         in Your documentation and require those who build Interfaces
         on it to comply.

     (d) Prominence. The notice must be at least as prominent as the
         product's other legal or "About" information and no smaller
         than ordinary body text. Removing, obscuring, bypassing, or
         making the notice materially less prominent is a material
         breach of this License.

     (e) Source distributions. Source distributions must carry an
         equivalent notice in the NOTICE file, the README, and a
         prominent place in the program.

     (f) No substitution claims. You must not present the Work, a
         Derivative Work, or their Outputs as a substitute for a
         proficient, authorized teacher.

2.2  ISLAMIC SHARIA COMPLIANCE

     Islamic Sharia is the source of law for the Work and its Derivative
     Works. Every use, modification, distribution, and deployment must
     adhere to the rulings of Islamic Sharia. Any use not adhering to
     those rulings is unlicensed and a material breach of this License.
     This Section is incorporated as a contractual condition within
     applicable law.

2.3  COMMERCIAL USE CONDITIONS

     Commercial use, commercial distribution, and charging fees for the
     Work or Derivative Works are permitted, subject to paragraphs (a)
     and (b):

     (a) NO ADVERTISEMENTS. This paragraph applies to everyone, whether
         or not the use is commercial. The Work, Derivative Works, and
         every Covered Product must never include Advertisements, and
         must never include or run advertisement-serving code,
         advertisement attribution or conversion-measurement code for
         advertising campaigns, cross-app or cross-site tracking for
         advertising purposes, or code that sells or shares End User
         data for advertising purposes. General analytics and crash
         reporting are not prohibited, provided they are not used for
         any of these purposes. This paragraph does not prohibit:

           (i)   informing End Users of Your own products and services;
          (ii)   accepting donations, and acknowledging donors or
                 sponsors by name without promotional content;
         (iii)   charging the fees contemplated by paragraph (b);
          (iv)   offering, for a fee or commission, human teaching
                 services that You or the teacher provide, provided there
                 is no paid placement or paid ranking; or
           (v)   Advertisements shown by a third-party hosting or
                 distribution platform (such as a download site or
                 package mirror) outside the Interface and not under
                 Your control.

     (b) FREE ACCESS FOR THOSE WHO CANNOT PAY. If You charge any fee to
         End Users for access to the Work, a Derivative Work, or a
         Covered Product (including subscriptions, one-time purchases,
         or paywalls), You must also provide a clear, easy-to-access,
         no-cost method of using the Essential Functionality:

           (i) automatically, with no request by the End User and no
               verification of the End User's circumstances, for End
               Users located in economies classified by the World Bank
               as "Low income" or "Lower-middle income" in the
               classification in effect on the date of access. You may
               determine location by commercially reasonable methods
               (such as IP address, app-store region, or device locale)
               and may rely on them in good faith. If location cannot
               be determined, path (ii) must be offered; and

          (ii) for individuals anywhere who cannot afford the fee,
               through a simple path reachable inside the application
               interface (for example, self-declaration or a community
               code, meaning a code issued by You, a community, or an
               institution that unlocks free access), without intrusive
               verification, means-testing, or the need to contact
               support.

         The free path must be visible to the End User before any
         payment is requested. An End User is not "charged" if a school,
         employer, or other institution pays on their behalf and they
         pay nothing themselves.

2.4  NO REMOVAL OF THE ADDITIONAL CONDITIONS

     You may add Your own license terms for Your modifications, or for
     Derivative Works as a whole, provided the resulting terms preserve
     the Additional Conditions in Section 2 in full force. Every
     distribution of the Work or Derivative Works must reproduce this
     License in full, including Appendix A.

2.5  TERMINATION

     Notwithstanding the word "irrevocable" in Sections 2 and 3 of the
     Base License, if You breach this License and do not cure the
     breach within thirty (30) days after the earlier of (i) written
     notice from the Licensor or any Contributor, or (ii) the time You
     become aware of it, all licenses granted to You under this License
     terminate automatically. If You cure the breach within that
     period, Your licenses remain in force. Each person who receives
     the Work or a Derivative Work from You receives a license directly
     from the Licensor and Contributors on the terms of this License;
     termination of Your licenses does not terminate the licenses of
     recipients who comply with this License.

2.6  SEVERABILITY

     If any provision of this License is held invalid or unenforceable,
     it shall be reformed to the minimum extent necessary to make it
     enforceable, and the remaining provisions shall remain in full
     force.

2.7  ACCEPTANCE

     By using, reproducing, modifying, distributing, or making
     available the Work, a Model, or a Derivative Work (including by
     downloading or running a Model), You accept this License. The
     Licensor may require an explicit acceptance step, such as a gated
     download, for the Model.

